[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: GBSK UCSI Test Protocol
UID: DHF-GBSK-UCSI-0003-TP
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-ucsi

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This protocol defines the minimum verification tests for the GBSK UCSI Software Requirements Specification, DHF-GBSK-UCSI-0001.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Test Configuration

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless a test specifies otherwise, execute it on a fully assembled GBSK system in its approved service/test configuration. A bench test uses the machine PCBs on a bench without machine peripherals.

Manual X-ray emission testing shall be performed only by qualified personnel under the approved radiation-safety procedure and in the approved service/test configuration.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
===================  ==========================================
Abbreviation/Term    Definition
===================  ==========================================
GCB                  Gryphon Control Board
HVPS                 High Voltage Power Supply
UCSI                 GBSK technician-facing service interface
===================  ==========================================
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TP-UCSI-
TITLE: Test Cases

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TP-UCSI-001
TITLE: UCSI deployment, telemetry sessions, status, and version information
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that UCSI presents current telemetry, status, operational logs, and version information; supports numerical and graphical monitoring, recording, and replay; and preserves the preceding five minutes of live telemetry in operator-requested and automatic fault CSV exports in both supported deployment modes.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Bench test setup with the GCB and HVPS telemetry channels available, known GCB and HVPS firmware versions, and the ability to publish controlled active-fault sets. The setup can supply continuously changing, time-correlated telemetry for at least six minutes and safely introduce and clear test faults.

The standalone UCSI application and the system PC application containing the hosted UCSI module are installed with known CNC software versions. Remove or inventory pre-existing UCSI CSV exports before each deployment-mode run.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the standalone UCSI application, connect the bench test setup, and begin the continuously changing telemetry stream.
2. Confirm that current operating-parameter values, communication status, system status, interlock status, and active faults are displayed.
3. Confirm that the displayed GCB firmware, HVPS firmware, and CNC software versions match the installed versions.
4. Select a telemetry parameter for the monitored-parameter list and for a graph; confirm that its current numerical value and telemetry history are displayed.
5. Start and stop a telemetry recording, load the recorded session, and verify play, pause, timeline seeking, and return to live monitoring.
6. After telemetry has run for at least six minutes, request a CSV export. Confirm that its rows cover only samples received during the five minutes preceding the request, include the changing values expected in that interval, and exclude earlier samples. Confirm that the header contains UTC timestamp, elapsed time, live sequence, and every available telemetry parameter.
7. With no active fault, safely introduce one test fault. Confirm that exactly one new, uniquely named fault-tagged CSV is created and that it contains only the five minutes of telemetry preceding the fault report with the columns checked in step 6.
8. Publish the same active-fault set again and confirm that no duplicate CSV is created. Add a second test fault while the first remains active and confirm that exactly one separate, uniquely named CSV is created for the second fault.
9. Clear the first fault, then safely introduce it again and confirm that exactly one new CSV is created for the recurrence.
10. Save the displayed operational logs. Confirm that the saved log contains the displayed entries and that the operational log records each successful automatic telemetry export with its sample count and output filename.
11. Close the standalone application, start the system PC application, and open the hosted UCSI module.
12. Repeat steps 2 through 10.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
In both deployment modes, UCSI displays the current system operating parameters, communication status, system status, interlock status, active faults, operational logs, and installed software versions. A selected parameter appears numerically and in its telemetry-history graph. Recording and replay support play, pause, seek, and return to live operation. Operator-requested and automatic fault CSV files contain every telemetry column and only samples from the five minutes immediately preceding their respective trigger; older samples are absent. Each transition to a newly active fault creates one separate, uniquely named fault-tagged CSV, unchanged active faults create none, and a cleared fault creates another when it recurs. The operational log identifies each successful automatic export.
<<<
